| The simplest cycle: a handler emitting to itself. Rejected before the
| program runs, in both output modes — recursion is what would let a chain
| of handler calls overflow the stack, so the language does not have it.
Down { n } => {
    emit Down { n = n - 1 } to this get inner
    return Done { value = 0 }
}
emit Down { n = 3 } to this
